OL,3,GNEWSAResidents object to stadium music
OL,4,Aevent over noise
OL,5,
OL,6,FPeople living on the opposite side of
OL,7,Fthe river to a football stadium have
OL,8,Fobjected to a music event planned
OL,9,Fthere.
OL,11,FThe house music event is due to take
OL,12,Fplace at the Gateshead International
OL,13,FStadium on the 30 and 31 October, with
OL,14,Flocal DJ Ben Hemsley performing to
OL,15,Fabout 6,000 ravers over both days.
OL,17,FBut residents on the other side of the
OL,18,FRiver Tyne have raised concerns over an
OL,19,Fentertainment and alcohol licence
OL,20,Fapplication made to Gateshead Council
OL,21,Ffor the event.
OL,23,APub: 16-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,397,390,260,160,0,100
